{"step_index":142,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:50:51Z","thinking":"**Initiating monotonicity proof**\n\nMonotonicity needs to be established for the general case where *k* is less than or equal to *m*. Starting an inductive proof on *m* with a base case.\n\n\n**Analyzing walk-ballWithin relationship**\n\nExamining `Walk` definition, the `cons` constructor prepends an edge. Induction on the `Walk` is considered to prove that if walk length is less than or equal to *k*, then the endpoint is in the ball. The induction step needs to show how a longer walk relates to ball membership. Symmetry of the adjacency relation is relevant.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"grep_search","args":{"CaseInsensitive":false,"MatchPerLine":true,"Query":"def reverse","SearchPath":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/lean_project/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph","toolAction":"Searching the web","toolSummary":"Grep def reverse in SimpleGraph"}}]}
