{"step_index":145,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:50:57Z","thinking":"**Reasoning about graph walk induction**\n\nConsider induction on graph walks to demonstrate membership within a bounded ball. The base case, a nil walk, establishes that the start node equals the end node and thus lies within the ball of radius 0. For the inductive step, examine a walk constructed from an adjacency and a shorter walk.\n\nAssuming the induction hypothesis for the shorter walk, the intermediate node lies within a smaller ball. The symmetry of the adjacency then establishes that the start node of the original walk is within a ball one unit larger, leveraging a relevant lemma about the successor function within `mem_ballWithin`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Add walk to ballWithin connection lemmas","EndLine":32,"Instruction":"Add mem_ballWithin_of_walk lemmas","ReplacementContent":"lemma mem_ballWithin_succ_of_adj {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n    (k : ℕ) (v u w : V) (hu : u ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G k v) (hadj : G.Adj u w) :\n    w ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G (k + 1) v := by\n  dsimp [GraphCalc.ballWithin]\n  apply Finset.mem_union_right\n  apply Finset.mem_biUnion.mpr\n  refine ⟨u, hu, ?_⟩\n  rw [Finset.mem_filter]\n  exact ⟨Finset.mem_univ w, hadj⟩\n\nlemma mem_ballWithin_of_walk_reverse {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n    {v w : V} (q : G.Walk w v) : w ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G q.length v := by\n  induction q with\n  | nil =>\n    rw [ballWithin_zero, SimpleGraph.Walk.length_nil]\n    exact Finset.mem_singleton_self v\n  | cons hadj q' ih =>\n    rw [SimpleGraph.Walk.length_cons]\n    exact mem_ballWithin_succ_of_adj G q'.length v _ w ih hadj.symm\n\nlemma mem_ballWithin_of_walk {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n    {v w : V} (p : G.Walk v w) : w ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G p.length v := by\n  have h := mem_ballWithin_of_walk_reverse G p.reverse\n  rw [SimpleGraph.Walk.length_reverse] at h\n  exact h","StartLine":22,"TargetContent":"lemma mem_ballWithin_succ_of_adj {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n    (k : ℕ) (v u w : V) (hu : u ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G k v) (hadj : G.Adj u w) :\n    w ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G (k + 1) v := by\n  dsimp [GraphCalc.ballWithin]\n  apply Finset.mem_union_right\n  apply Finset.mem_biUnion.mpr\n  refine ⟨u, hu, ?_⟩\n  rw [Finset.mem_filter]\n  exact ⟨Finset.mem_univ w, hadj⟩","TargetFile":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc/Challenge_2a2555cc.lean","toolAction":"Editing file","toolSummary":"Add mem_ballWithin_of_walk lemmas"}}]}
